{"name":"Shopping Bag","hex":"#5a4743","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shopping bag","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A strong bag with handles used to put purchases in; usually made of plastic, paper or fabric, sometimes given away with a purchase."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shopping_bag"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shopping Bag","blocks":[{"text":"Shopping Bag is the fifth studio album by TV-linked pop project The Partridge Family. Released in March 1972, just as the second season of the TV series was finishing in North America, the album entered Billboard's Top LP's chart in late March, peaking at no. 18 in late April. The album remained in the Top 200 for 17 weeks and was certified gold. The vinyl release of the album contained a novelty plastic shopping bag."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2d/Shopping_Bag_-_The_Partridge_Family.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shopping_Bag","wikidata":"Q16204794"},{"title":"Shopping bag","blocks":[{"text":"Shopping bags are medium-sized bags, typically around 10–20 litres in volume, that are used by shoppers to carry home their purchases. Some are intended as single-use disposable products, though people may reuse them for storage or as bin liners, etc.; others are designed as reusable shopping bags."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/EatonsShoppingBag1997.JPG/330px-EatonsShoppingBag1997.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shopping_bag","wikidata":"Q1778351"},{"title":"Shopping","blocks":[{"text":"Shopping is an activity in which a customer examines or looks for the available goods or services presented by one or more retailers with the potential intent to purchase a suitable selection of them or casually browses such items without actual intent to purchase. \"Shopping\" as a word in English is a gerund derived from Old English \"sċoppa,\" meaning \"shed,\" \"booth,\" \"stall,\" or \"shop.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Souk_in_Tunisia_1.jpg/330px-Souk_in_Tunisia_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shopping","wikidata":"Q830036"},{"title":"Bag","blocks":[{"text":"A bag, also known regionally as a sack or tote, is a common tool in the form of a floppy container, typically made of cloth, leather, bamboo, paper, or plastic. The use of bags predates recorded history, with the earliest bags being lengths of animal skin, cotton, or woven plant fibers, folded up at the edges and secured in that shape with strings of the same material. Bags can be used to carry items such as personal belongings, groceries, tools, and other objects. They come in various shapes and sizes, often equipped with handles or straps for easier carrying."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Bolsas-de-asa-plana-interior-bolsapubli.jpg/330px-Bolsas-de-asa-plana-interior-bolsapubli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bag","wikidata":"Q1323314"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Carrets_de_la_compra.jpg/500px-Carrets_de_la_compra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Carrets_de_la_compra.jpg/1280px-Carrets_de_la_compra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Carrets_de_la_compra.jpg/500px-Carrets_de_la_compra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wheeled bag/Shopping trolley (caddy)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarrets_de_la_compra.jpg"},{"s